From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Bates <stephen.bates@amd.com>
Date: 2026-07-30
Subject: [PATCH 11] fix: fallback when store() Event.from_ipc_handle fails (ROCm)

LMCacheDrivenTransferModule.store() reconstructs a CUDA Event from
the IPC handle bytes sent by vLLM alongside each STORE request, then
calls vllm_event.wait(stream) to ensure vLLM has finished writing the
KV blocks before the server copies them.

On ROCm 7.14 / gfx950 (MI355X), Event.from_ipc_handle() raises
hipErrorInvalidValue immediately (the same platform bug addressed by
patch 10 in futures.py).  The exception propagates out of the affinity
pool worker thread, is caught by mq._notify_response(), and logged as:

  LMCache ERROR: Error in blocking handler
    torch.AcceleratorError: CUDA error: invalid argument (hipErrorInvalidValue)

The store uses all-or-nothing semantics: if the worker raises, the ZMQ
response signals an error and the entire store request is dropped.
Those chunks are therefore never committed to L1 or L2, so subsequent
prefetch lookups for them produce:

  lmcache_mp_l2_prefetch_failure_chunks_total = 191  (in job 15939)

despite 2,332 chunks being written to the NVMe pool.  This is the
primary cause of the low L2 hit rate.

Fix: catch any exception from from_ipc_handle and fall back to
torch.cuda.synchronize(device) — a full device sync that guarantees
the vLLM write has completed before we copy.  Slower (blocks the
entire GPU vs. one stream) but correct; the fallback only fires on
ROCm platforms where IPC events are broken.

Observed: SPUR MI355X gfx950, ROCm 7.14, LMCache v0.5.2, cliff job
15939 — l2_prefetch_failure_chunks_total=191, l2_prefetch_hit=54.

Applies after patches 01-10.
---
--- a/lmcache/v1/multiprocess/modules/lmcache_driven_transfer.py
+++ b/lmcache/v1/multiprocess/modules/lmcache_driven_transfer.py
@@ -1030,10 +1030,23 @@
                     "handles (Event.from_ipc_handle not available). "
                     "Multiprocess IPC requires CUDA."
                 )
-            vllm_event = torch_dev.Event.from_ipc_handle(
-                cache_context.device, event_ipc_handle
-            )
-            vllm_event.wait(stream=cache_context.stream)
+            try:
+                vllm_event = torch_dev.Event.from_ipc_handle(
+                    cache_context.device, event_ipc_handle
+                )
+                vllm_event.wait(stream=cache_context.stream)
+            except Exception:
+                # HIP IPC events are broken on some ROCm platforms (e.g. gfx950/ROCm 7.14):
+                # from_ipc_handle raises hipErrorInvalidValue immediately after export.
+                # Fall back to a full device synchronise so the vLLM KV write
+                # completes before we copy.  Slower but correct; without this the
+                # store is silently dropped (all-or-nothing semantics), leaving
+                # chunks absent from L2 and producing spurious prefetch failures.
+                logger.warning(
+                    "Event.from_ipc_handle failed (hipErrorInvalidValue on ROCm?); "
+                    "falling back to torch.cuda.synchronize() for store ordering."
+                )
+                torch_dev.synchronize(cache_context.device)
 
             # CPU-synchronous sentinel: a GPU store is about to be enqueued.
             # Must be published via publish() (not publish_on_stream) so the
